vering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)","title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph: from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sides), Z is the set of vertices reached from the free left vertices by alternating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths, an edge not in the matching from left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left vertices, so it does not depend on the matching. O(m √n)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum vertex cover (exact): "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" minus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":", in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (τ = n − α, Gallai). Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once. The cost is "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Deterministic, but which minimum cover it is depends on the search; for one fixed by a rule,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()","title":"minimumVertexCover()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover()","type":"topic"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumEdgeCover()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumEdgeCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum edge cover (positions, ascending), or nil when some vertex has no edge: the edges of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumMatching()"},{"text":", then for each vertex still uncovered, in vertex order, its first edge in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order (a self-loop covers its vertex). n − ν edges (Gallai)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n · m · log n)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumedgecover()","kind":"symbol","title":"minimumEdgeCover()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumEdgeCover()","type":"topic"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumVertexCover()":{"type":"topic","ab